@SassyDecay Now, hold on there, Buddy.

Red Barrels has been replacing the Assets they made with AI with actual Work from REAL Developers.
They not only started doing this during the Early Release but also when AI wasn't seen to be a Threat.

@TrueAIHound Is what you are saying that our brain doesn't start with pattern matching  , it starts by modeling the real world? then turning that model into recognition shortcuts through long term memory, and that process is what actually makes us capable of understanding new things.

And that perception is not pixel or text based like what's being used in current AI, but is based on other types of sensors, like movement and idk what else our eyes can do.

I'm not sure I understood you correctly, but makes alot of sense. I always believed that the current design of AI is incapable of intelligence, it's more like an advanced search engine, if it's not in the weights it can't understand it, although it can pretend to. I didn't know the perception vs recognition could be the key to solving that. I wish you all the luck with your research.

@TheRealAdamG Thanks for engaging. 

I think it’s very reasonable to say you think it’s very unlikely. But I really don’t understand the second half of your post, why do you feel so strongly?  Do you have any evidence that I’m conscious? Why should someone who doesn’t have the same priors as you be barred from accessing model weights? 

To be clear I’m generally extremely skeptical of anyone who makes strong claims that models are conscious as well. I just don’t think we understand consciousness enough to make strong claims either way.
